1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,474
The river had taught them to publish the weak numbers; the city would teach them who pays for them.

2
00:00:05,474 --> 00:00:15,231
The ninth arc opened with a blow to the city budget and a question that was not relevant to the election: who pays for the water treatment plant?

3
00:00:15,231 --> 00:00:24,100
A presidential briefing, a congressional hearing, and a budgetary review had all been scheduled for the same morning.

4
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:28,664
“The favourite answer is a slogan,” the mayor said.

5
00:00:28,664 --> 00:00:32,264
“The feasible one is a fare.”

6
00:00:32,264 --> 00:00:36,273
The signal was a banknote and a coin on the table.

7
00:00:36,273 --> 00:00:41,527
“Enforcement without a receiver is theft,” the treasurer said.

8
00:00:41,527 --> 00:00:57,465
“Comply or pay, but someone has to collect.” A basketball court, a tennis court, and a volleyball court had been promised in the same document, and the basket of revenue was empty.

9
00:00:57,465 --> 00:01:01,859
The briefing was authoritative and the grammar was flawless.

10
00:01:01,859 --> 00:01:06,959
“We must rid the budget of the habitual exception,” she said.

11
00:01:06,959 --> 00:01:21,681
“A privileged chimney and an ordinary one should undergo the same inspection.” The elephant in the room was the candidacy of the deputy mayor, whose moody indifference to the numbers was well known.

12
00:01:21,681 --> 00:01:29,780
A bystander at the hearing asked the only grammatical question of the day: who is the subject of this sentence?

13
00:01:29,780 --> 00:01:38,028
A persistent leftist on the council, a prayer group, and a burial society all asked the same thing.

14
00:01:38,028 --> 00:01:43,562
“A sin is not a line in a budget,” one of them said.

15
00:01:43,562 --> 00:01:49,771
The proposal was to facilitate the collection of a small fee and to discard the rest.

16
00:01:49,771 --> 00:01:58,330
“If we err, we should err on the side of the poor,” the mayor said, with more grace than the room expected.

17
00:01:58,330 --> 00:02:05,229
A coin, a banknote, and a basket of receipts were passed around the table.

18
00:02:05,229 --> 00:02:12,798
The next step was a public register of every exemption, published while the process was still open.

19
00:02:12,798 --> 00:02:19,847
It was the first signal that the trade-off would be visible, and the room went quiet for a while.

20
00:02:19,847 --> 00:02:28,640
Everyone between the two sides needed a while to agree, and almost nobody wanted to go into the water question again.

21
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:37,864
The air in the room was thick; the land values, the process, and the stars of the evening news were all on the same page.

22
00:02:37,864 --> 00:02:45,817
Thus the need for a public register became obvious to us, and someone at the back began to write it down.

23
00:02:45,817 --> 00:02:54,349
Within the hour, the favorite proposal was to purify the water fairly and to share the cost.
